# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# Frontend toolchain (docs/Superseded/PLAN-webgl-renderer.md). Only the INSTALL tree is
# ignored -- `package-lock.json` is tracked, and so is the build output at
# static/vendor/renderer.bundle.js. That artifact is committed deliberately, so
# a fresh clone plus `cargo run` serves a working viewer with no node
# installed; CI rebuilds it and fails on any diff, because a committed
# generated file with no gate drifts silently and the failure it produces is a
# stale renderer with no error anyone can act on.
node_modules/

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# roommate is a Rust crate that uses src/bin/ for multiple binaries (cargo's
# own convention) -- unignore it from the [Bb]in/ rules above, which are
# meant for .NET build-output directories, not Rust source directories.
!src/bin/

# The snapshot store is local runtime data -- ignored, with ONE deliberate
# exception: the House A sample set is published so a fresh clone has real
# pushed data to run against (26 rooms, two snapshots, ~300 KB). Every other
# project under data/snapshots is somebody's local push and stays out.
#
# Git cannot re-include a path whose parent directory is excluded, so the
# exception has to be unpicked one level at a time -- hence the alternating
# exclude/negate pairs below rather than a single `!data/snapshots/House A/`.
data/*
!data/snapshots/
data/snapshots/*
!data/snapshots/House A/
# Anywhere, not just /scripts: the extractor is Python too, and running it (or
# anything that imports it) drops a __pycache__ beside the source that a
# `git add -A` will otherwise happily commit.
__pycache__/

# NOT ignored, deliberately: `.mcp.json` (the Claude Code MCP registration for
# bin/mcp.rs) is tracked. It used to be listed here, which silently contradicted
# docs/mcp-host-setup.md's "committed at the crate root, so opening Claude Code
# in the roommate directory picks it up automatically" -- a fresh clone simply
# got no roommate tools. It is safe to track because it holds no secret and no
# machine-specific path: it invokes `cargo run -q --bin mcp` with settings paths
# relative to the crate root. Keep it that way; an absolute path belongs in the
# host's own config (that doc's Claude Desktop section), never in this file.
settings/projects/RHH.toml
